      "writtenOn": "2022-11-01T21:40:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately no, usage being 64 bits is enshrined in both SDK \u0026 NDK APIs, so changing that is highly non-trivial. We only just crossed the 32-bits mark with USAGE_FRONT_BUFFER so I expected to have a while yet before this was a concern - if you\u0027re already seeing usage bit exhaustion mind taking to a bug and we can discuss solutions there?",
      "parentUuid": "77491aa6_25497d1b",
